// Serialization built on `std.quirks`' generic `To<T>`/`From<T>`. A type
// that converts to/from `str` (e.g. `impl TomlDoc as From<str>`) is what
// serializable means here — there's no separate `Serialize`/`Deserialize`
// quirk, and the same primitive generalizes to other target types (e.g.
// `std.json` targets `JsonValue`).
// 
// ```
// To<str> s = &doc;
// str text = to_string(s);
// ```
// 
// For structured, typed (de)serialization of your own compounds, see
// `std.quirks`'s `To<JsonValue>`/`From<JsonValue>`. Fun has no reflection or
// derive macros, so each type hand-implements the conversion.

imp std.quirks;

// Convert any `To<str>` implementer to text.
pub fun to_string(To<str> value) str {
  ret value.to();
}

// Decode text into any `From<str>` implementer.
pub fun from_string(From<str> value, str input) {
  value.from(input);
}
